  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a function fff, define f1(x)=f(x)f^1(x) = f(x)f1(x)=f(x) and fm(x)=f(fm−1(x))f^m(x) = f(f^{m - 1}(x))fm(x)=f(fm−1(x)) for all m&gt;1m &gt; 1m&gt;1.\n\nYou are given 222 integers NNN and KKK.\n\nFind the number of functions f:{1,2,3,…,N+K}→{1,2,3,…,N+K}f : \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, N + K\\} \\rightarrow \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, N + K\\}f:{1,2,3,…,N+K}→{1,2,3,…,N+K} satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\nf(x)=xf(x) = xf(x)=x for all x&gt;Nx &gt; Nx&gt;N.\nfN(x)&gt;Nf^N(x) &gt; NfN(x)&gt;N for all xxx.\nfN(x)≤fN(x+1)f^N(x) \\le f^N(x + 1)fN(x)≤fN(x+1) for all 1≤x&lt;N1 \\le x &lt; N1≤x&lt;N.\nSince the answer may be large, print it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of functions modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\le K \\le 10^91≤K≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
